{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794424861,"nonce":"CYMXVUviJioWNGDxA++Ghb65eWk=","title":"CPPIA is untested: a scriptable host does not build on this macOS SDK","message":"A CPPIA script cannot call C++, so a binding reaches it through a host: an\nhxcpp program built with `-D scriptable` that carries the library's\ngenerated classes and hxn's own, and runs the script with\n`cpp.cppia.Host`. The script is compiled against the host's\n`export_classes.info`, which leaves those classes out of it. Nothing in the\ngenerated classes should need changing for that: the script only calls\ntheir public methods, and `raw` and the extern class stay inside the host.\n\nTried on macOS with hxcpp 4.3.2 and the fixture's generated classes:\n\n    haxe -cp \u003chost dir\u003e -cp haxe -cp \u003cgen\u003e/haxe/cpp -main Host -cpp host \\\n      -D scriptable -D dll_export=export_classes.info \\\n      --macro \"include('hxn')\" Counter Job Tally ... \\\n      -D HXN_INCLUDE=include -D COUNTER_INCLUDE=\u003cgen\u003e/include \\\n      -D COUNTER_LIB=target/debug/libcounter_gen.a\n\nHaxe compiles it and writes export_classes.info. The C++ build then fails\nin hxcpp's own bundled zlib 1.2.11, which a scriptable host links and an\nordinary program here does not: `zutil.h` defines `fdopen` as a macro, and\nthe macOS 26 SDK's `_stdio.h` declares a function of that name. That is\nhxcpp's to fix or to be built around, not hxn's.\n\nNot tried: a newer hxcpp, a Linux host (the NUC has no hxcpp), a define\nthat drops zlib from a scriptable host.\n\nOnce a host builds, what is left is a `gen-cppia` mode for\ntests/counter/run.sh (build the host, compile haxe/Generated.hx with\n`-cppia` and `-D dll_import`, run it), and deciding whether `hxn run`\ngrows a `cppia` target that builds both.","files":null}]}